    "details": "Plack project reports:\n\n> \\[SECURITY\\]\n>\n> - Fix memory leak of every request env in Plack::Middleware::Recursive\n>   (CVE-2026-110333)\n> - Plack::Request::Upload-\\>basename never returns \\'\\', \\'.\\' or\n>   \\'..\\' (CVE-2026-110332)\n> - Plack::App::URLMap matches SERVER_PORT literally when stripping it\n>   from Host (CVE-2026-110335)\n>\n> \\[BUG FIXES\\]\n>\n> - Plack::Middleware::ErrorDocument restores the env after a\n>   subrequest, so outer middleware such as AccessLog sees the original\n>   request (CVE-2026-110334)\n>\n> \\[BUG FIXES\\]\n>\n> - Document that Plack::Handler::FCGI and Apache2 keep dot segments in\n>   PATH_INFO and warn against relying on front-server path-based access\n>   control (CVE-2026-110336)\n",
    "id": "FreeBSD-2026-0513",
